    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.70). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Ryan Johnson. His dynamic platoon advantage against the right-hander, paired with the potential for elite production from the two-hole, makes him the engine of the lineup. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Andy Pages** (74.01) provide significant value; while **Jackson Merrill** faces a slight drag due to his opponent's ability to control the running game, his matchup against JR Ritchie is highly favorable for run production. **Kyle Tucker** remains an automatic start despite a neutral platoon, as his raw power and consistent approach against Kendry Rojas provide a stable floor.\n\nStrategic focus shifts to **Jacob Wilson** (69.38), whose score is inflated by a 5% boost from wind-aided conditions and an 11% skill advantage against Robbie Ray. He narrowly edges out **Josh Jung** (54.92) for the final utility spot. The optimizer favored **Jacob Wilson** due to the favorable wind metrics and a superior matchup profile; **Josh Jung** was the last cut, ultimately sidelined because he faces a stiffer challenge in Sandy Alcantara and lacks the specific platoon leverage required to surpass our higher-scoring infield options. We are also monitoring **Drake Baldwin** and **Brayan Rocchio** closely, as their scores remain tentative pending the release of confirmed lineups.\n\nWhile the outlook is strong, we must acknowledge the \"Lineup Pending\" risk across the roster. **Dominic Smith** sits at a marginal 43.87; while he is currently in the lineup, his low score makes him the primary candidate to be pulled for a bench reserve like **Miguel Vargas** should the official order shift unfavorably. Furthermore, the 1.89s pop time from the opposing catcher against **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** presents a slight headwind for our stolen base efficiency. Managers should keep a close watch on weather reports for any late-breaking delays, as the high-scoring potential of the middle order relies heavily on stable, favorable hitting conditions in the projected park environments.",
